Table full name: bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_speciation_daily_summary
Column name: state_code Type: STRING Description: The FIPS code of the state in which the monitor resides.
Column name: county_code Type: STRING Description: The FIPS code of the county in which the monitor resides.
Column name: site_num Type: STRING Description: A unique number within the county identifying the site.
Column name: parameter_code Type: INT64 Description: The AQS code corresponding to the parameter measured by the monitor.
Column name: poc Type: INT64 Description: This is the “Parameter Occurrence Code” used to distinguish different instruments that measure the same parameter at the same site.
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: The monitoring site’s angular distance north of the equator measured in decimal degrees.
Column name: longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: The monitoring site’s angular distance east of the prime meridian measured in decimal degrees.
Column name: datum Type: STRING Description: The Datum associated with the Latitude and Longitude measures.
Column name: parameter_name Type: STRING Description: The name or description assigned in AQS to the parameter measured by the monitor. Parameters may be pollutants or non-pollutants.
Column name: sample_duration Type: STRING Description: The length of time that air passes through the monitoring device before it is analyzed (measured). So, it represents an averaging period in the atmosphere (for example, a 24-hour sample duration draws ambient air over a collection filter for 24 straight hours). For continuous monitors, it can represent an averaging time of many samples (for example, a 1-hour value may be the average of four one-minute samples collected during each quarter of the hour).
Column name: pollutant_standard Type: STRING Description: A description of the ambient air quality standard rules used to aggregate statistics. (See description at beginning of document.)
Column name: date_local Type: DATE Description: The calendar date for the summary. All daily summaries are for the local standard day (midnight to midnight) at the monitor.
Column name: units_of_measure Type: STRING Description: The unit of measure for the parameter. QAD always returns data in the standard units for the parameter. Submitters are allowed to report data in any unit and EPA converts to a standard unit so that we may use the data in calculations.
Column name: event_type Type: STRING Description: Indicates whether data measured during exceptional events are included in the summary. A wildfire is an example of an exceptional event; it is something that affects air quality, but the local agency has no control over. No Events means no events occurred. Events Included means events occurred and the data from them is included in the summary. Events Excluded means that events occurred but data form them is excluded from the summary. Concurred Events Excluded means that events occurred but only EPA concurred exclusions are removed from the summary. If an event occurred for the parameter in question, the data will have multiple records for each monitor.
Column name: observation_count Type: INT64 Description: The number of observations (samples) taken during the day.
Column name: observation_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: The percent representing the number of observations taken with respect to the number scheduled to be taken during the day. This is only calculated for monitors where measurements are required (e.g., only certain parameters).
Column name: arithmetic_mean Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average (arithmetic mean) value for the day.
Column name: first_max_value Type: FLOAT64 Description: The highest value for the day.
Column name: first_max_hour Type: INT64 Description: The hour (on a 24-hour clock) when the highest value for the day (the previous field) was taken.
Column name: aqi Type: INT64 Description: The Air Quality Index for the day for the pollutant, if applicable.
Column name: method_code Type: INT64 Description: An internal system code indicating the method (processes, equipment, and protocols) used in gathering and measuring the sample. The method name is in the next column.
Column name: method_name Type: STRING Description: A short description of the processes, equipment, and protocols used in gathering and measuring the sample.
Column name: local_site_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the site (if any) given by the State, local, or tribal air pollution control agency that operates it.
Column name: address Type: STRING Description: The approximate street address of the monitoring site.
Column name: state_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the state where the monitoring site is located.
Column name: county_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the county where the monitoring site is located.
Column name: city_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the city where the monitoring site is located. This represents the legal incorporated boundaries of cities and not urban areas.
Column name: cbsa_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the core bases statistical area (metropolitan area) where the monitoring site is located.
Column name: date_of_last_change Type: DATE Description: The date the last time any numeric values in this record were updated in the AQS data system.
